WEBVTT

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:07.450
As we cast our eyes above to the boundless sky, we know

00:00:08.410 --> 00:00:15.500
Whatever tomorrow brings, the sun will always shine

00:00:16.250 --> 00:00:19.590
So won't you come with me?

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:36.650
It's almost time for the school bell to ring

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.860
And every moment by moment

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:41.280
I feel more and more like I could fly

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:44.740
This feeling fills my thoughts and sets my heart alight

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:48.200
It's this moment I love most of all

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:52.870
In my bag I hold all the things I've overcome

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.630
And on their wings, I'll fly into the future

00:00:56.630 --> 00:01:01.130
We can do anything, at any time and any place

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.630
And no one can stop us even if they try

00:01:04.800 --> 00:01:09.260
From ING and that alone can we proceed

00:01:09.390 --> 00:01:13.180
Carrying all our feelings as we go

00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:17.190
Flying with our dreams for all to see

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:23.650
Let's close today's chapter, and start a new page!

00:02:06.780 --> 00:02:09.700
This is the best way to practice distance shooting.

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:11.740
Today, we're practicing our long range shooting.

00:02:11.990 --> 00:02:17.460
We're attempting to fire ten rounds into the vitals of a human silhouette target 500 meters away.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:24.550
Sig-chan's shots are the best.

00:02:24.630 --> 00:02:26.880
She hits it right in the center.

00:02:27.340 --> 00:02:28.470
Yeah...

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:36.810
We're most accurate between the ranges of 400 and 500 meters.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:46.240
She might even be able to hold her own with the higher caliber upperclassmen in the high school division.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:47.360
Well, that's because

00:02:47.650 --> 00:02:51.240
Switzerland's full of mountains!

00:02:52.330 --> 00:02:54.740
And...

00:02:56.830 --> 00:02:59.170
When you're shooting from one mountain ridge to the next,

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.750
you need to be able to aim over that distance.

00:03:01.750 --> 00:03:04.460
Switzerland is so cool!

00:03:05.670 --> 00:03:09.050
Are you sure we should be leaving Sig-chan to fire rounds all by herself?

00:03:09.050 --> 00:03:10.220
It's fine.

00:03:10.220 --> 00:03:12.430
She's an expert at long range shooting, anyway.

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:16.220
Elle couldn't hit a target that far away even if she spent all day.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.390
Besides, we're all the same caliber.

00:03:19.390 --> 00:03:20.600
No one'll be able to tell.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:22.940
You don't think I can tell?!

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:24.570
He could tell.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:27.530
Sure, the SG550 is the same caliber as you,

00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:31.030
but it uses a special GP90 bullet.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.830
No way... Why did this happen?

00:03:33.830 --> 00:03:35.160
How about I answer that?

00:03:36.200 --> 00:03:39.330
If I used the same NATO rounds as you,

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:41.790
I wouldn't be as accurate.

00:03:43.210 --> 00:03:44.960
Tell us that in the first place...

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:47.960
What? You never asked.

00:03:48.380 --> 00:03:51.010
If I'd known that, I would've come up with a different scheme for cutting class.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:53.680
You guys!

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.400
I've come as you requested.

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.530
I'm sorry for bothering you when you're so busy.

00:04:09.530 --> 00:04:12.910
It sure is a heap of trouble to have a sister like that.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:13.780
Not at all.

00:04:15.160 --> 00:04:17.740
They're the ones who're gonna have all the trouble.

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:18.620
Huh?

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.960
And now, the results from our midterms.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:28.550
So, Funko...

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:30.300
What is it, Sixteen-san?

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:32.130
I challenge you to a duel!

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:32.840
Right here!

00:04:34.180 --> 00:04:35.140
I'm right here...

00:04:47.900 --> 00:04:48.780
Almost...

00:04:49.400 --> 00:04:51.400
matches our scores on the shooting.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:56.820
Looks like skipping out on long range shooting practice really hurt us.

00:04:56.820 --> 00:04:57.950
Where were you, Sig-chan?

00:04:57.950 --> 00:04:58.910
I ranked third.

00:04:58.910 --> 00:05:01.620
Wow. I wish I was third.

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:05.540
I bet we're gonna have to take remedial classes.

00:05:05.540 --> 00:05:06.830
Well, that's fine.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.000
We'll just have to go to a few extra sessions.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:10.510
How naive.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.920
Way too naive.

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.430
Fourteen-nee and

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:15.840
Fal-neechan?!

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:21.350
You'll be stuck in remedial classes until you get perfect scores on all your make-up tests.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:23.890
What are you talking about?

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:26.270
We'll never be able to do that in 300 years.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.520
That's where we come in.

00:05:27.520 --> 00:05:29.480
Time for the bonus round.

00:05:29.480 --> 00:05:31.940
If you beat us, you'll be exempt from all your remedial lessons.

00:05:33.360 --> 00:05:35.530
It's on, Funko.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:43.620
I guess I've gotten pretty used to all this.

00:05:50.090 --> 00:05:51.800
A battlefield...

00:05:54.970 --> 00:05:56.090
What are you doing?!

00:05:56.470 --> 00:05:57.890
Put it away!

00:05:58.760 --> 00:06:00.560
Put it away now!

00:06:00.850 --> 00:06:02.100
What are you doing?! We need—

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:03.140
Shut up!

00:06:03.140 --> 00:06:05.060
You don't need ammunition in my class!

00:06:18.490 --> 00:06:20.370
It's on, Funko.

00:06:20.370 --> 00:06:22.910
Either steal our flag

00:06:22.910 --> 00:06:25.000
or get wiped out trying.

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:27.620
Our battlefield will be the school grounds.

00:06:27.620 --> 00:06:29.080
The game will begin after classes.

00:06:29.580 --> 00:06:31.340
The 4:00 chime will be the starting signal.

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.090
Hey, Funko.

00:06:38.470 --> 00:06:42.260
It's your fault he hates guns so much now.

00:06:42.260 --> 00:06:43.600
Yeah, but...

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.930
I believe we're in the middle of class.

00:06:47.230 --> 00:06:48.100
Yes...

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:49.190
Ouch.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:55.940
There's two of them and three of us.

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:58.030
Our range is a bit limited...

00:06:58.280 --> 00:07:01.120
But if we work together, we should be able to do it.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.330
So, where's the flag?

00:07:03.330 --> 00:07:05.290
Funko, Elle, let's go.

00:07:05.290 --> 00:07:06.080
Right.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.420
It's common sense to figure out what you need to know first,

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:17.800
but they are going up against our sisters.

00:07:21.390 --> 00:07:23.430
Okay, let's go over the rules.

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:28.180
In order to win, we have to take their flag or pop their balloons.

00:07:28.180 --> 00:07:32.270
If our balloons are popped, we lose.

00:07:33.230 --> 00:07:34.230
Right.

00:07:34.570 --> 00:07:35.230
Okay.

00:07:35.230 --> 00:07:38.190
Let's beat 'em so we can forget about those remedial classes!

00:07:38.190 --> 00:07:39.110
Roger!

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.070
Go!

00:07:59.050 --> 00:08:01.180
This'll be our first challenge.

00:08:01.180 --> 00:08:03.260
We have to clear this hill in order to get to the high school,

00:08:03.260 --> 00:08:06.470
so we won't be able to move all that quickly, and there's a sizable distance to the building.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:10.560
They'd be able to see us clearly from there, so we'd be sitting ducks.

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:15.400
Instead, we're gonna forget the stairs and follow the fence here, climbing up on this side.

00:08:16.270 --> 00:08:19.860
The trees here will cover us from fire from the school.

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:21.650
Let's go.

00:08:22.320 --> 00:08:23.200
This way.

00:08:24.870 --> 00:08:26.870
Watch out for branches.

00:08:26.870 --> 00:08:30.580
If your balloon got caught on one and popped, it'd be pretty...

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:33.750
Elle!

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:35.040
No, no!
Elle!

00:08:35.040 --> 00:08:35.420
Elle!

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:38.960
Sniper fire!

00:08:40.460 --> 00:08:41.920
Where are they firing from?!

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:43.050
Can they see us?!

00:08:44.050 --> 00:08:46.550
Hey Elle, what are you doing?!

00:08:46.550 --> 00:08:47.430
Don't...

00:08:51.180 --> 00:08:52.140
Wait...

00:08:52.850 --> 00:08:53.980
They're behind us?

00:08:54.770 --> 00:08:56.560
Elle should be out,

00:08:56.770 --> 00:08:58.230
but she's still assisting.

00:08:58.230 --> 00:08:59.820
She's gonna get in trouble for that.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.030
The old middle school building!

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:01.990
Damn.

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:08.120
Sixteen-chan?!

00:09:08.120 --> 00:09:10.490
Fourteen must have come up with this plan!

00:09:10.790 --> 00:09:13.620
Funko, get to the high school while I handle this!

00:09:13.620 --> 00:09:16.000
When I fire, that's your signal.

00:09:16.960 --> 00:09:20.090
It's about 200 meters to the old building from here.

00:09:20.090 --> 00:09:24.010
I have to be within 100 meters for my burst to be effective.

00:09:24.970 --> 00:09:29.720
A burst is when three consecutive shots are fired with every pull of the trigger.

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:31.720
It's short for burst mode.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:35.730
It was developed as a means to prevent running out of bullets as quickly as with full auto fire.

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:43.690
Seishou Academy is an elementary school, a middle school, and a high school combined.

00:09:43.690 --> 00:09:46.820
Your school placement depends entirely on what type of ammunition you use.

00:09:47.070 --> 00:09:50.280
The 7.62x51mm rounds used in the high school division are

00:09:50.280 --> 00:09:53.950
more powerful and have better range than their middle school counterparts,

00:09:53.950 --> 00:09:56.210
but they cause more recoil when fired.

00:09:56.210 --> 00:09:58.290
Guns using these rounds are difficult to control in full auto and

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:00.250
have trouble hitting more than one precise target.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:05.590
The assault rifles in the middle school use lighter ammunition than their high school counterparts.

00:10:05.590 --> 00:10:07.430
Not only are they easier to control while firing,

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:10.010
they also allow you to carry more rounds.

00:10:10.010 --> 00:10:12.850
This gives each soldier the chance to take out more targets effectively.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:13.810
However,

00:10:14.060 --> 00:10:18.400
because each round is so light, more energy is lost due to air resistance during flight,

00:10:18.400 --> 00:10:20.230
and since the wind affects the trajectory of each bullet,

00:10:20.230 --> 00:10:24.070
they're not very effective for hitting targets over 300 meters away.

00:10:24.320 --> 00:10:26.950
So, for a round used in the middle school to hit with any precision,

00:10:26.950 --> 00:10:29.280
the target generally has to be within 100 meters.

00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.240
In other words,

00:10:30.240 --> 00:10:34.660
the battle started with the high school division having an overwhelming advantage.

00:10:35.000 --> 00:10:37.330
If I can get inside the high school building,

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:39.000
my range disadvantage won't matter.

00:10:40.330 --> 00:10:42.130
That's the sound of a three-round burst.

00:10:42.130 --> 00:10:43.300
It must be Sixteen-san!

00:10:43.590 --> 00:10:44.380
Engage!

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.770
<i>It's Fal-neechan.</i>

00:11:44.150 --> 00:11:45.690
<i>She's on the other side of this wall...</i>

00:11:52.160 --> 00:11:53.950
Sorry, Funko.

00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:58.080
You think there's only two of us, don't you?

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:04.630
Goodbye,

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:06.380
Funko-chan.

00:12:13.390 --> 00:12:14.390
G3?!

00:12:16.180 --> 00:12:17.890
Now you've done it!

00:12:26.480 --> 00:12:27.360
<i>It can't be...</i>

00:12:27.820 --> 00:12:29.860
<i>Sniping from the middle school?</i>

00:12:30.280 --> 00:12:31.400
<i>That can only mean...</i>

00:12:32.610 --> 00:12:34.660
So you showed up after all...

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:36.660
Sig!

00:12:37.080 --> 00:12:38.290
Sorry about that.

00:12:38.290 --> 00:12:40.200
I decided to join the fun at the last minute.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:42.790
Huh? Why is Sig here?

00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.050
Now, Sixteen!

00:12:48.300 --> 00:12:49.170
Right!

00:12:49.170 --> 00:12:51.220
I owe you one, Sig!

00:12:58.970 --> 00:13:01.020
Damn kids.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:07.230
You're not the only one with full auto!

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:12.650
Where are you aiming, Fourteen-nee?!

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:13.740
Shut up!

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.670
Shoot and move.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:30.170
A basic sniping tactic.

00:13:32.420 --> 00:13:33.090
Sig!

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:45.890
A grouping of three shots within 8 centimeters, all in the space of two seconds.

00:13:46.520 --> 00:13:48.270
That's G3-senpai for you.

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:06.080
This is going to make great practice, G3-senpai.

00:14:08.580 --> 00:14:11.090
Let's do this, Sig.

00:14:12.250 --> 00:14:16.930
I'll show you who's the top sniper around here.

00:14:17.220 --> 00:14:18.340
G3...

00:14:18.840 --> 00:14:21.640
Isn't she following the plan?

00:14:21.640 --> 00:14:22.510
Man...

00:14:38.280 --> 00:14:41.580
<i>If Fal-neechan and Fourteen-san are over there,</i>

00:14:41.870 --> 00:14:44.790
<i>that means no one's guarding the flag on the second floor.</i>

00:14:47.410 --> 00:14:49.000
Here I come, flag!

00:15:00.390 --> 00:15:02.010
No!!

00:15:02.010 --> 00:15:02.970
No, no, no!

00:15:02.970 --> 00:15:04.680
No! No! No!!

00:15:05.850 --> 00:15:08.020
Oh yeah, I forgot to mention that.

00:15:08.020 --> 00:15:10.100
The clubhouse is under construction right now,

00:15:10.100 --> 00:15:13.360
so the soccer club is using our classroom to change.

00:15:13.980 --> 00:15:16.530
So the flag isn't there.

00:15:16.530 --> 00:15:19.660
You need to figure out what the flag is and where it might be.

00:15:20.740 --> 00:15:22.660
This is a game where the flag moves.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:24.620
You see,

00:15:24.870 --> 00:15:26.750
I am the flag.

00:15:37.300 --> 00:15:40.630
<i>If I get Fourteen all worked up and make her use all her bullets,</i>

00:15:40.630 --> 00:15:42.340
we'll have a real chance of winning this.

00:15:45.010 --> 00:15:48.140
This is the end, Sixteen.

00:15:49.310 --> 00:15:49.940
Huh?

00:15:50.600 --> 00:15:53.810
Have you finally lost it, Fourteen-nee?!

00:15:53.810 --> 00:15:55.940
No! Look up!

00:15:56.190 --> 00:15:57.190
Up?

00:15:59.950 --> 00:16:00.780
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:00.780 --> 00:16:01.740
Make it go pop!
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.370
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:03.370 --> 00:16:04.280
Make it go pop!
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:04.280 --> 00:16:06.330
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:07.160
Make it go pop!
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:07.160 --> 00:16:09.250
We're going to get your balloon!

00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:11.160
Ch-Chestnuts!

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.960
And you thought I was nuts!

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.840
That pun was terrible! You're giving me goosebumps!

00:16:16.840 --> 00:16:17.750
Shut up!

00:16:17.750 --> 00:16:19.380
I don't care!

00:16:21.720 --> 00:16:23.680
We're gonna get your balloon!

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.600
N-No way...

00:16:26.050 --> 00:16:28.560
I don't want to lose to Fourteen...

00:16:29.100 --> 00:16:30.980
Maybe that dog can help me get up onto the <i>woof</i>.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.980
No! Doggie!

00:16:33.810 --> 00:16:36.150
I just <i>dove</i> that bird.

00:16:36.150 --> 00:16:38.070
Birdie!

00:16:38.610 --> 00:16:41.280
<i>I'm tired of these terrible puns!</i>

00:16:41.280 --> 00:16:42.990
<i>I don't want to lose to her!</i>

00:16:42.990 --> 00:16:46.410
Chestnut bump!

00:17:05.890 --> 00:17:06.390
Ouch!

00:17:06.390 --> 00:17:06.800
Ouch!

00:17:06.800 --> 00:17:07.180
Ouch!

00:17:07.180 --> 00:17:07.470
Ouch!

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:08.470
Ow! Ow!

00:17:08.470 --> 00:17:10.350
C-Critical hit...

00:17:10.850 --> 00:17:14.560
Ouch! Ow! Ow! Ouch!!

00:17:14.560 --> 00:17:15.400
Ouch!!

00:17:15.400 --> 00:17:16.230
Ouch!!

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:16.900
Ouch!!

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:18.900
I see.

00:17:18.900 --> 00:17:20.030
Understood.

00:17:29.450 --> 00:17:29.870
Yes?

00:17:30.120 --> 00:17:32.000
<i>Fourteen got a double KO.</i>

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:33.870
<i>How are things going over there, G3?</i>

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.250
She's tough.

00:17:35.670 --> 00:17:38.250
<i>If you can keep Sig busy, that should be enough.</i>

00:17:38.960 --> 00:17:40.170
Got it.

00:17:52.520 --> 00:17:55.600
At this distance, we're on a level playing field, Fal-neechan!

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:59.690
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

00:18:01.610 --> 00:18:02.780
Why you...

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:05.700
They're not hitting her...

00:18:06.030 --> 00:18:07.530
Understand now?

00:18:07.530 --> 00:18:10.160
We're not equally matched.

00:18:10.160 --> 00:18:12.410
The 7.62x51mm rounds we use

00:18:12.410 --> 00:18:15.080
have a payload of about 180 grains.

00:18:15.410 --> 00:18:18.630
The payload of your bullets is only 62 grains,

00:18:18.630 --> 00:18:20.130
making them unable to maintain

00:18:20.130 --> 00:18:21.500
their trajectory when pitted against the water.

00:18:22.000 --> 00:18:24.420
As long as you're trapped on the other side of that fountain,

00:18:24.420 --> 00:18:26.840
I have a huge advantage.

00:18:26.840 --> 00:18:27.680
In that case...

00:18:30.510 --> 00:18:33.020
Did you think I'd just let you jump out from there?

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:40.020
<i>I don't want to lose to Fal...</i>

00:18:40.020 --> 00:18:43.780
<i>But there's no easy way out of this situation.</i>

00:18:44.360 --> 00:18:45.490
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:18:47.280 --> 00:18:48.660
Checkmate.

00:18:49.160 --> 00:18:50.740
Just give up.

00:18:54.370 --> 00:18:56.750
What are you going to do?

00:19:13.220 --> 00:19:16.730
I'll congratulate you on managing to graze my balloon.

00:19:17.100 --> 00:19:18.730
You didn't just give up,

00:19:18.730 --> 00:19:20.440
you kept moving forward.

00:19:20.980 --> 00:19:22.810
Don't forget that.

00:19:23.150 --> 00:19:24.480
Fal-neechan...

00:19:35.080 --> 00:19:38.120
I guess when it comes down to it, we're all really similar, aren't we?

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:39.710
Yeah, we really are.

00:19:39.710 --> 00:19:41.330
I don't like that...

00:19:43.670 --> 00:19:46.670
I worked up a sweat.

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:51.300
I haven't had fun like that after school in a while.

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:58.230
I found out later that the game was our remedial course, designed to test how good we really were,

00:19:58.730 --> 00:20:02.020
and we didn't have to take any extra classes.

00:20:02.480 --> 00:20:04.190
Besides Elle-chan, that is.

00:20:04.690 --> 00:20:08.690
Yeah, having all your shots in a 20 cm spread is pretty tough.

00:20:08.690 --> 00:20:11.110
My sister ends up having a spread more than 10 meters wide.

00:20:11.110 --> 00:20:13.160
Wow.

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:17.790
I wonder how G3-senpai was minimizing the recoil from her full auto.

00:20:18.660 --> 00:20:22.790
Those girls have no idea how much trouble we go through.

00:20:23.210 --> 00:20:26.550
We talked to the teachers to get them out of remedial lessons.

00:20:26.550 --> 00:20:29.210
Those girls have talent.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.340
They just aren't very motivated.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:32.630
That's why I thought

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:36.430
it'd be good if we put them in a situation where they had to motivate themselves.

00:20:36.680 --> 00:20:39.180
You're too kind to your sister, Fal.

00:20:39.180 --> 00:20:41.270
I don't need you telling me that.

00:20:41.270 --> 00:20:43.150
You totally wanted in.

00:20:43.150 --> 00:20:46.440
G3, how did you enjoy your fight with Sig?

00:20:46.730 --> 00:20:48.650
She's got good senses.

00:20:48.650 --> 00:20:51.280
She made me play my trump card.

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:53.030
You went that far?

00:20:53.030 --> 00:20:54.870
Something that shameless?

00:20:54.870 --> 00:20:56.490
What is it?

00:20:56.910 --> 00:20:59.290
A secret technique to keep recoil down.

00:20:59.290 --> 00:21:00.750
A secret technique?! Really?!

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:03.960
Y-You told me to keep her busy,

00:21:03.960 --> 00:21:05.750
so I didn't have a choice!

00:21:05.750 --> 00:21:06.790
What did you do?

00:21:06.790 --> 00:21:08.590
I wanna know too.

00:21:08.590 --> 00:21:10.630
C-Could we just drop it, please?

00:21:10.630 --> 00:21:14.380
Come on. Come on. Tell me.

00:21:14.380 --> 00:21:16.010
Please, G3!

00:21:16.300 --> 00:21:18.760
But you don't have a bipod.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:21.020
You need a bipod for this trick.

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:23.390
I'll put one on! I'll force it on if I have to!

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.730
Take off your socks first.

00:21:26.980 --> 00:21:28.360
Uh, okay.

00:21:32.110 --> 00:21:32.940
Now,

00:21:33.990 --> 00:21:35.910
put the gun barrel here like this,

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:37.820
and keep your body like this.

00:21:37.820 --> 00:21:39.780
W-Wait...
Then raise your legs like this.

00:21:39.990 --> 00:21:41.700
Okay, that's it.

00:21:41.700 --> 00:21:43.080
Try shooting.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:54.670
T-This is...

00:21:57.140 --> 00:21:58.510
embarrassing!

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:06.980
Let's tear another page off our calendar

00:22:08.020 --> 00:22:14.530
Together we braved

00:22:18.990 --> 00:22:26.460
past ages and never-ending conflict

00:22:26.750 --> 00:22:34.090
Together we laughed and cried in those hectic times

00:22:34.970 --> 00:22:39.720
When I ran

00:22:42.600 --> 00:22:53.110
I put my footsteps into the ground

00:22:54.190 --> 00:23:00.870
Let's rip another page off our calendar

00:23:01.830 --> 00:23:08.040
Something is bound to change

00:23:09.420 --> 00:23:16.170
One by one the days I ripped off pile up

00:23:16.670 --> 00:23:20.050
like a past I cannot erase

00:23:20.510 --> 00:23:26.220
They will be my strength for days to come

00:23:30.900 --> 00:23:31.770
Bath time!

00:23:31.770 --> 00:23:33.400
Funko-chan is going off to bathe.

00:23:33.400 --> 00:23:34.480
I want to join her

00:23:34.480 --> 00:23:36.280
and scrub her down.

00:23:36.280 --> 00:23:36.940
Next time:

00:23:36.940 --> 00:23:37.650
Wash it!

00:23:37.650 --> 00:23:38.320
Scrub it!

00:23:38.320 --> 00:23:39.360
Watch it!
